<h2 class="wp-block-heading tt-h2 tt-isec__h">The four trips, told</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:group {"className":"tt-trips__wrap sp-reveal sp-reveal--up","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group tt-trips__wrap sp-reveal sp-reveal--up"><!-- wp:html -->
<div class="tt-trips__row tt-trips__row--tall"><a class="tt-card tt-card--tall" href="/trips/"><span class="tt-card__fig"><img src="<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'assets/images/trip-porto-river.webp' ) ); ?>" alt="Students and a teacher on a riverside terrace above a wide river and an iron bridge." width="864" height="1152" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><span class="tt-chips tt-chips--card"><span class="tt-chip tt-chip--box">Porto</span><span class="tt-chip tt-chip--pill">Geography</span></span></span><h3 class="tt-card__t">Porto river and coast</h3><p class="tt-card__m">Year 10 · 4 nights · 84 students</p><p class="tt-card__p">Designed for Year ten geography students, this four-night study tour travels by air to northern Portugal. Eighty-four students and nine leaders study river basin dynamics along the Douro and measure coastal erosion patterns along Atlantic beaches. Fieldwork sessions are paired with urban studies in the historic port city, investigating historic trade infrastructure, transport links, and modern municipal regeneration. Students document findings daily in field notebooks before evening group analyses at the hostel.</p></a><a class="tt-card tt-card--tall" href="/trips/"><span class="tt-card__fig"><img src="<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'assets/images/trip-normandy-beach.webp' ) ); ?>" alt="Students and a teacher on a wide flat beach at low tide." width="864" height="1152" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><span class="tt-chips tt-chips--card"><span class="tt-chip tt-chip--box">Normandy</span><span class="tt-chip tt-chip--pill">History</span></span></span><h3 class="tt-card__t">Normandy coast history</h3><p class="tt-card__m">Year 8 · 3 nights · 42 students</p><p class="tt-card__p">This three-night residential for Year eight history classes travels by coach and ferry across the Channel. Forty-two students and four leaders explore the nineteen forty-four Allied landing beaches, coastal battery fortifications, and memorial sites. In Bayeux, pupils participate in a curated museum workshop examining the nine-hundred-year-old embroidery to understand medieval narrative art and political messaging. The tour concludes with coastal walks and structured diary reflections at the hostel.</p></a><a class="tt-card tt-card--tall" href="/trips/"><span class="tt-card__fig"><img src="<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'assets/images/trip-naples-ruins.webp' ) ); ?>" alt="Sixth-form students walking among ancient ruins with a volcano on the horizon." width="864" height="1152" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><span class="tt-chips tt-chips--card"><span class="tt-chip tt-chip--box">Naples</span><span class="tt-chip tt-chip--pill">Classics</span></span></span><h3 class="tt-card__t">Bay of Naples classics and geology</h3><p class="tt-card__m">Sixth form · 5 nights · 36 students</p><p class="tt-card__p">A five-night air tour tailored for thirty-six sixth-form classics and geology students accompanied by four leaders. The group explores the preserved streets and domestic architecture of Pompeii alongside guided volcanic fieldwork on Mount Vesuvius. Pupils study seismic strata, classical archaeology, and urban preservation, connecting physical landscape formations directly to ancient historical records. Daily fieldwork is supervised by experienced subject leaders with extensive regional experience.</p></a><a class="tt-card tt-card--tall" href="/trips/"><span class="tt-card__fig"><img src="<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'assets/images/trip-seville-host.webp' ) ); ?>" alt="A student with a host mother at a tiled kitchen table, an exercise book open." width="864" height="1152" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><span class="tt-chips tt-chips--card"><span class="tt-chip tt-chip--box">Seville</span><span class="tt-chip tt-chip--pill">Spanish</span></span></span><h3 class="tt-card__t">Seville language week</h3><p class="tt-card__m">Year 9 · 7 nights · 28 students</p><p class="tt-card__p">Our seven-night Spanish immersion tour takes twenty-eight Year nine pupils and three leaders to Andalusia by air. Students reside with vetted local host families in pairs, enjoying authentic home meals and practising conversational Spanish in daily domestic life. Each morning, pupils attend structured language lessons focused on vocabulary and dialogue, followed by afternoon cultural visits through historic neighbourhoods, markets, and regional heritage sites.</p></a></div>
